# Ghost Chains – AML Risk Scoring Service (Phase 3)

## Features
- Full compliance with Phase 1, 2, and 3 requirements
- Stateful graph with 24‑hour lookback window
- Idempotent transaction processing
- Risk scores combining structural, identity, and value signals
- Clean API endpoints: `/health`, `/reset`, `/transactions`

## Setup

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
Run locally
bash
uvicorn main:app --reload --port 8080
Test with cURL
bash
# Health
curl http://localhost:8080/ghost-chains/health

# Reset
curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/ghost-chains/reset -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"clearTransactions":true}'

# Send a transaction
curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/ghost-chains/transactions -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{
  "transactions": [
    {
      "txId": "tx1",
      "fromUserId": "meridian",
      "toUserId": "apex",
      "amount": 10000,
      "createdAt": "2026-06-08T12:00:00Z"
    }
  ]
}'
Deploy to Render
Create a new Web Service.

Build command: pip install -r requirements.txt

Start command: uvicorn main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port $PORT

Scoring Logic (summary)
Structural: cycles (+0.3), long paths (+0.1 per extra step), convergence/divergence (+0.15 each)

Identity: IP/device changes on same edge (+0.15 each)

Value: amount reversal (+0.3), high variance (+0.1)

Combined with weights: structural 0.5, identity 0.2, value 0.3, capped at 1.0

This gives a coherent model that ranks suspicious patterns higher.

text

